## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.11+
- Node.js 18+
- Gemini API Key ([Get one free](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey))

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/ai-compliance-investigator.git
cd ai-compliance-investigator
2️⃣ Backend Setup
bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# Mac/Linux
source venv/bin/activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
3️⃣ Configure Environment
Create .env in backend/:

env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./compliance.db
CHROMA_DB_PATH=./data/chroma_db
4️⃣ Initialize Database & Seed Data
bash
python scripts/init_db.py
python scripts/ingest_documents.py
python scripts/run_demo.py
5️⃣ Start Backend
bash
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
API Docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

6️⃣ Frontend Setup
bash
cd ../frontend
npm install
npm run dev
Visit http://localhost:5173 🎉

🎥 Demo Flow
Dashboard → See all incidents

Click "New Incident" → Fill form → Submit

Click "Start Investigation" → Watch live workflow

Knowledge Graph tab → See entity relationships

Interview tab → Chat with stakeholders (AI-simulated)

Report tab → Download final PDF report

📸 Screenshots
🎛️ Dashboard
https://docs/screenshots/dashboard.png

🔍 Live Investigation
https://docs/screenshots/investigation.png

🕸️ Knowledge Graph
https://docs/screenshots/graph.png

💬 Stakeholder Interview
https://docs/screenshots/interview.png

📄 Generated Report
https://docs/screenshots/report.png

🔌 API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/incidents	Create new incident
GET	/api/incidents	List all incidents
POST	/api/investigations/start	Start investigation
GET	/api/investigations/{id}	Get investigation status
WS	/ws/investigations/{id}	Live workflow stream
POST	/api/interviews/{id}/message	Send interview message
GET	/api/graph/{incident_id}	Get knowledge graph
GET	/api/reports/{id}	Get final report
POST	/api/documents/upload	Upload policy document
Full API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

🧪 Testing
bash
cd backend
pytest tests/ -v

cd frontend
npm run test
🎓 What I Learned
Building multi-agent systems with tool use

Combining RAG + Knowledge Graph for hybrid reasoning

Designing state-machine workflows for autonomous agents

Streaming real-time AI updates via WebSockets

CPU-efficient AI architecture (no GPU dependency)

Explainable AI — logging every decision with reasoning

